  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Initial release of the PublicFunction.Converter library for safe and efficient data type conversion in C#.\n\n      ✨ Key Features in this version:\n      -Conversion support for primitive data types including: Boolean, Byte, Char, Decimal, Double, Float, Guid, Integer, Long, Short, UInt, ULong, UShort, and String\n      - Specialized services for structured data conversion including DateTime, DataSet, DataTable, and Json\n      - Automatic error handling and full support for Nullable Types\n      - Standardized method naming conventions for consistent To/From type conversion\n      - Reduced runtime errors through built-in validation mechanisms\n\n      📦 How to use:\n      Each class is specifically designed for a target data type.For example, use the IntegerService class methods to convert strings to integers.\n\n      📚 Complete documentation and usage examples are available in the project repository:\n      https://github.com/rayanabniro/PublicFunction/tree/main/PublicFunction.Converter",
